omments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:67183d6983a4df882629b29f9879ccea237afbac8f3ba2a1e4df81f72529df2f","file":"preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":29,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1a1603ece43319d7cddd0b5da19d3d7f56f0951ea2e225641e210d9233eaf0ff","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:67183d6983a4df882629b29f9879ccea237afbac8f3ba2a1e4df81f72529df2f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L29"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main-transitive}\nLet $V$ be a countable transitive model of $\\ZFC$. There are a set forcing\n$\\mathbb Q\\in V$, a $V$-generic filter $G$, and a transitive symmetric\nsubmodel $W$ of $V[G]$ such that\n\\[\n V\\subseteq W\\subseteq V[G],\\qquad\n \\Ord^W=\\Ord^V,\\qquad\n W\\models\\ZF+\\PP+\\ACwo+\\neg\\AC.\n\\]\nEvery countable sequence of elements of $V$ that belongs to $W$ already\nbelongs to $V$."}
